 third[13Gfrom the bottom and shows important messages.  The bottom two[9d lines show the most commonly used shortcuts in the editor.[10d[K[11d Shortcuts are written as follows: Control-key sequences are notated with[12d a '^' and can be entered either by using the Ctrl key or pressing the Esc[13d key twice.  Meta-key sequences are notated with 'M-' and can be entered[14d using either the Alt, Cmd, or Esc key, depending on your keyboard setup.[15d Also, pressing Esc twice and then typing a three-digit decimal number[16d from 000 to 255 will enter the character with the corresponding value.[17d The following keystrokes are available in the main editor window.[18d Alternative keys are shown in parentheses:[19d[K[20d^G     (F1)      Display this help text[21d^X     (F2)      Close the current buffer / Exit from nano[2d[22;31H(B[0;1m[37m[41m[ Unbound key: ^D ][39;49m(B[m[2d